{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-127736" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${Z}^{-1}$ where\n$Z=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127736" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nZ=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $Z$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Z}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(Z)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(Z)=1\\cdot 8-3\\cdot 2=2\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Z}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(Z)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z{Z}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {Z}^{-1}Z & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127736" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782"} {"question" "q-127736" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127736" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127736" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${C}^{-1}$, where\n$C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $C$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(C)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(C)=3\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 3=-3\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(C)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-3)}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C{C}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {C}^{-1}C & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782"} {"question" "q-127744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${U}^{-1}$, where \n$U=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $U$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(U)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(U)=-2\\cdot 7-(-5)\\cdot 3=1\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(U)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -(-5) & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U{U}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {U}^{-1}U & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782"} {"question" "q-127737" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127737" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127737" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-316780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${A}^{-1},$ where\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-316780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $A$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(A)=6\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 9=-12\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-12}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -9 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1/12 & 1/6 \\\\ 3/4 & -1/2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{A}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1/12 & 1/6 \\\\ 3/4 & -1/2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {A}^{-1}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1/12 & 1/6 \\\\ 3/4 & -1/2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-316780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782"} {"question" "q-316780" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-316780" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{12}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-316780" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-316780" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-316780" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-316780" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${B}^{-1}$, where \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $B$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(B)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(B)=2\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 1=-1\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(B)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-1)}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B{B}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {B}^{-1}B & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-11717" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nH=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,J=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,K=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-11717" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $H$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(H)=5\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 0=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(H)=0,$ we conclude that $H$ is not invertible. Since $H$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $H$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $J$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(J)=2\\cdot 6-3\\cdot 4=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(J)=0,$ we conclude that $J$ is not invertible. Since $J$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $J$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $K$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\nTherefore, only $H$ and $J$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-11717" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782"} {"question" "q-11717" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-11717" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$H$ and $J$ only"] ["text" "$H$ and $K$ only"] ["text" "$H$ only"] ["text" "$J$ and $K$ only"] ["text" "$J$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-11717" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$H$ and $J$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- The matrix $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)=0,$ we conclude that $C$ is not invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $C$ do not have an inverse." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $B$ only"] ["text" "$A$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$A$ only"] ["text" "$B$ only"] ["text" "$C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ and $C$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nS=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -6\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $S$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(S)=1\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 0=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(S)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $S$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $T$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot (-6)-4\\cdot (-3)=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(T)=0,$ we conclude that $T$ is not invertible. Since $T$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $T$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $U$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(U)=0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1)=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(U)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $U$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $T$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$S$ and $U$ only"] ["text" "$S$ only"] ["text" "$T$ and $S$ only"] ["text" "$T$ only"] ["text" "$U$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$T$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-7915" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-7915" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $P$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(P)=4\\cdot 6-8\\cdot 3=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(P)=0,$ we conclude that $P$ is not invertible. Since $P$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $P$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $Q$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Q)=1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1)=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Q)=0,$ we conclude that $Q$ is not invertible. Since $Q$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $Q$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $R$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\nTherefore, only $P$ and $Q$ are singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-7915" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782"} {"question" "q-7915" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-7915" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$P$ and $Q$ only"] ["text" "$P$ and $R$ only"] ["text" "$P$ only"] ["text" "$Q$ and $R$ only"] ["text" "$Q$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-7915" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$P$ and $Q$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 6 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Y=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- The matrix $X$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Y$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Y)=6\\cdot 6-7\\cdot 5=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Y)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Y$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Z$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Z)=(-2)\\cdot 5-10\\cdot 1=-20.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Z)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Z$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $X$ does not have an inverse." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$X$ and $Y$ only"] ["text" "$X$ and $Z$ only"] ["text" "$X$ only"] ["text" "$Y$ only"] ["text" "$Z$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$X$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $M=[\\begin{aligned}t & 4 \\\\ t & 10\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $M$ is singular if and only if $det(M)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =t\\cdot 10-t\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =10t-4t \\\\  & =6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6t & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $t$ is $t=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "t=-5"] ["math" "t=-\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "t=0"] ["math" "t=5"] ["math" "t=\\frac{3}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "t=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-316781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}2x & 5x-1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-316781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(2x)\\cdot (-2)-4\\cdot (5x-1) \\\\  & =-4x+4-20x \\\\  & =-24x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-24x+4 & =0 \\\\ 24x & =4 \\\\ x & =\\frac{4}{24} \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-316781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782"} {"question" "q-316781" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-316781" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-11719" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $F=[\\begin{aligned}3 & t \\\\ t & 3\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-11719" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $F$ is singular if and only if $det(F)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(F) & =3\\cdot 3-t\\cdot t \\\\  & =9-{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9-{t}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =9 \\\\ t & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $t$ are $t=\\pm 3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-11719" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782"} {"question" "q-11719" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-11719" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "t=-3"] ["math" "t=2"] ["math" "t=3"] ["math" "t=\\pm 2"] ["math" "t=\\pm 3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-11719" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "t=\\pm 3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-71967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $V=[\\begin{aligned}7 & y \\\\ 5 & y\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-71967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $V$ is singular if and only if $det(V)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(V) & =7\\cdot y-5\\cdot y \\\\  & =7y-5y \\\\  & =2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y & =0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $y$ is $y=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-71967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782"} {"question" "q-71967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-71967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-1"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "y=0"] ["math" "y=1"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-71967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127905" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $P=[\\begin{aligned}n & -4 \\\\ -16 & n\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $n.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127905" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $P$ is singular if and only if $det(P)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =n\\cdot n-(-16)\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & ={n}^{2}-64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}-64 & =0 \\\\ {n}^{2} & =64 \\\\ n & =\\pm 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $n$ are $n=\\pm 8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127905" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782"} {"question" "q-127905" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127905" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "n=10"] ["math" "n=\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "n=\\frac{3}{5}"] ["math" "n=\\pm 4"] ["math" "n=\\pm 8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "q-127905" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "n=\\pm 8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e6524007a0939f99afc74fed4364eacad0a7381f47cc17e7d672052db9926cd"} {"question" "e-4502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $A^{-1},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/example-4502.json" "file_sha256" "d90d1dc48691d5c8e6cd79aaa9450e15416a1c0437b2e49a41de506ae4054a06"} {"question" "e-4502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a $2 \\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $A$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\det(A) = 1 \\cdot 1 - 0 \\cdot (-2) = 1\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}]. \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -0 \\\\ -(-2) & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{A}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {A}^{-1}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/example-4502.json" "file_sha256" "d90d1dc48691d5c8e6cd79aaa9450e15416a1c0437b2e49a41de506ae4054a06"} {"question" "e-4503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/example-4503.json" "file_sha256" "c5231f1b59cd38e29c467d9e0c7ea837116f3d696d9cd56f0255d2f4b94f850c"} {"question" "e-4503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\n\\det({A})=1 \\cdot 1 - 1 \\cdot 1 = 0.\n$$\n\nBecause $\\det(A)=0,$ we conclude that $A$ is not invertible. Since $A$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $A$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\n\\det({C})=3 \\cdot 3 - (-3) \\cdot 3 = 18.\n$$\n\nBecause $\\det(C) \\neq 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/example-4503.json" "file_sha256" "c5231f1b59cd38e29c467d9e0c7ea837116f3d696d9cd56f0255d2f4b94f850c"} {"question" "e-4504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If \n$[\\begin{aligned}1-k & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1-k\\end{aligned}]$\n is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/example-4504.json" "file_sha256" "34fa14c36f2c4f3a517ce126819d1d70167f169e288fc03290cd6aa8867b1cee"} {"question" "e-4504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $\\det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =(1-k)(1-k)-4 \\\\  & ={k}^{2}-2k-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2}-2k-3 & =0 \\\\ (k-3)(k+1) & =0 \\\\ k & =3,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $k$ are $k=3$ and $k=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/example-4504.json" "file_sha256" "34fa14c36f2c4f3a517ce126819d1d70167f169e288fc03290cd6aa8867b1cee"}] "usage" {"e-4502" [] "e-4504" [] "e-4503" []} "basis" 765 "retractions" [[17592186087443 :question/problem "Calculate $A^{-1}$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186087443 :question/worked-solution "Given a $2 \\times 2$ matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nthe inverse of $A$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA^{-1} &= (1)/(det(A))\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\det(A) = 1 \\cdot 1 - 0 \\cdot (-2) = 1\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA^{-1} &= (1)/(det(A))\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix}. \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -0 \\\\ - (-2) & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAA^{-1} &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= I_{2}✓ \\\\\nA^{-1}A &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= I_{2}✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186087444 :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186087444 :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n$\\det({A})=1 \\cdot 1 - 1 \\cdot 1 = 0$.\nBecause $\\det(A)=0$, we conclude that $A$ is not invertible. Since $A$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $A$ is singular.\n- The matrix $B$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n$\\det({C})=3 \\cdot 3 - (-3) \\cdot 3 = 18$.\nBecause $\\det(C) \\neq 0$, we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is singular."] [17592186087445 :question/problem "If\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 - k & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 - k\\end{bmatrix}$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $k$."] [17592186087445 :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $\\det(A)=0$. Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A) &= (1 - k)(1 - k) - 4 \\\\\n&= k^{2} - 2k - 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nk^{2} - 2k - 3 &= 0 \\\\\n(k - 3)(k + 1) &= 0 \\\\\nk &= 3,-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $k$ are $k=3$ and $k=-1$."]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
